1
00:00:00,103 --> 00:00:04,737
Clues in a Radio Drama In a radio drama a sheriff received

2
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:08,697
a report that a burglar had tried to steal an antique A

3
00:00:08,711 --> 00:00:12,250
watchful guard heard a clatter saw a figure flee and called a

4
00:00:12,263 --> 00:00:17,026
patrol The suspected outlaw left a badge behind but it might have

5
00:00:17,039 --> 00:00:21,882
been fake A second scene introduced a notorious gangster and a rumour

6
00:00:21,895 --> 00:00:25,921
that he planned to kidnap a dealer The police could not detain

7
00:00:25,934 --> 00:00:30,882
someone merely because a frightening story sounded plausible They had to examine

8
00:00:30,895 --> 00:00:36,118
evidence and follow the required procedure The narrator mentioned a warrant without

9
00:00:36,132 --> 00:00:41,368
explaining its legal details At the climax the apparent villain turned out

10
00:00:41,382 --> 00:00:45,579
to be a witness The real motive involved greed and a failed

11
00:00:45,592 --> 00:00:50,329
attempt to smuggle stolen ware The story taught listeners to separate a

12
00:00:50,342 --> 00:00:55,592
clue from an assumption A dramatic voice can make a questionable explanation

13
00:00:55,605 --> 00:00:58,566
sound persuasive but suspense is not proof
